-- title:
--   Degree of the norm equals the sum of local multiplicities
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field and let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $K$, and assume that its affine coordinate ring $K[W]$ — the quotient of $K[X][Y]$ by the Weierstrass polynomial, a free $K[X]$-algebra of rank $2$ — is a Dedekind domain. Let $a \in K[W]$ be nonzero. Then the degree (`natDegree`) of the norm $N_{K[W]/K[X]}(a) \in K[X]$, regarded as an integer, equals the sum over all height-one primes $v$ of $K[W]$ of the $v$-adic multiplicity $\mathrm{count}_v$ of the principal fractional ideal generated by the image of $a$ in the function field $K(W)$, i.e. of the $v$-adic valuation of $a$; the sum is taken as a finite sum over the (possibly infinite) index type of the height-one spectrum, which is legitimate because only finitely many terms are nonzero. Thus the degree of the norm of $a$ counts, with multiplicity and with no residue-degree factors since $K$ is algebraically closed, the zeros of $a$ on the affine curve.
--
--   This is the affine half of the statement that a nonzero polynomial function on a nonsingular Weierstrass curve has as many zeros as poles, the pole order at the point at infinity being read off from the degree of the norm over $K[X]$. It underlies the construction of principal divisors and the computation of valuations of Weil functions on the curve.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassCurve_Affine_CoordinateRing_natDegree_norm_eq_finsum_count.lean

